This project is a Go port of DSRC (DNA Sequence Reads Compressor),
derived from and built to be byte-exact interoperable with the
original C++ implementation.

Original project
-----------------
DSRC — DNA Sequence Reads Compressor
Authors: Lucas Roguski and Sebastian Deorowicz
Homepage: http://sun.aei.polsl.pl/dsrc
Source:   https://github.com/refresh-bio/DSRC
License:  GNU General Public License v2

Please cite the following papers when using DSRC (or this port):

  Roguski, L., Deorowicz, S. (2014) DSRC 2: Industry-oriented
  compression of FASTQ files, Bioinformatics, 30(15):2213-2215.
  https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btu208

  Deorowicz, S., Grabowski, Sz. (2011) Compression of DNA sequences
  in FASTQ format, Bioinformatics, 27(6):860-862.
  https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btr014

This Go port
------------
This code was produced with the assistance of Claude Code by reading
and translating the original DSRC C++ source (algorithms, data
structures, and — for the internal/realdsrc package specifically —
its exact on-disk file format) into Go. See README.md for a detailed
package-by-package account of what was ported, what was verified
against real DSRC output, and what was intentionally left out of
scope.

